Android's front end has its own texts. cRMainMenu::Init (000697d4) labels the first
entry "Play" (.rodata 0x82f24); the PC keeps its Exit button, where Android shows the
OpenFeint logo. cRIntro::Init (000674f8) labels Postal "Postal Adventure" (0x835cc).
After the Pro galaxy, cRSplash::Init (0006aba4) reads "Holy Flying Snails!" (0x839c8)
and cRSplash::AI (0006a900) "That isn't humanly possible!" (0x83924) and "You're
totally awesome!" (0x83968), where the postal ending advertises Challenge Mode and
Time Trial. The PC layout keeps each text on one line, so Android's leading '>' line
breaks are left out.

